# Cloudflare Pages does not support 404 rewrites in _redirects, so a catch-all
# `/* /index.html 200` answers a missing hashed asset with the HTML shell. A
# browser holding a stale index.html then executes HTML as JavaScript and
# renders a blank page. List the real SPA routes instead, so that everything
# else — including /assets/ misses — falls through to 404.html.
#
# The rewrite target must be `/`, not `/index.html`: Pages normalises
# `/index.html` back to `/`, which turns these rules into 308 redirects and
# makes the splat rule look like an infinite loop, so Pages drops it.
/schemes / 200
/rankings / 200
/funds / 200
/fund-classes/* / 200
